id: pm-r3o7x4
title: "The related ceiling is pinned to the live count with block enforcement, so recording one associative sibling relation anywhere in the tracker fails CI while the share floor it duplicates would have allowed it"
description: "The raw related-edge ceiling is pinned to the observed count, so one legitimate associative link fails enforcement even when semantic composition improves. Govern associative growth by dilution ratio or explicit justified headroom, retain a negative control, and make addition-safe edge guidance discoverable before mutation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,assurance,governance,graph,ratchet
created_at: "2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-24T08:58:01.342Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-24T08:58:00.280Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-24T08:58:00.280Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Associative edge growth is governed by a composition ratio, so an addition that raises semantic share can never fail the associative bound; Any retained raw count bound declares explicit headroom and a rationale for the headroom, so it is not pinned to the observation that created it; A negative control proves the bound still fails an associative-only dilution pass and passes a mixed pass that raises semantic share; The two overlapping declarations are reconciled into one enforced quantity with the other demoted to reporting, recorded as a disposition on the owning item; Guidance for filing an item states which kinds are addition-safe, so an agent does not discover the constraint by failing a gate"
goal: explainable-graph
objective: "Associative growth is bounded by dilution rather than by count, so an honest sibling link is always recordable and a dilution pass is always refused"
value: Two declarations enforce the same intent with different strictness. The weaker-but-correct one measures dilution; the stronger one forbids a legitimate edit that dilutes nothing.
impact: "Every future item that records a sibling relation trips a block gate, so the cheapest compliant response is to leave real context unrecorded or to mislabel it as a semantic kind."
outcome: "Semantic share is the enforced quantity for composition; any raw associative count remains a reported diagnostic with declared headroom, never a zero-headroom block gate."
why_now: "Hit immediately: filing four well-linked findings this session took related from 6,053 to 6,063 and turned two block gates red, with semantic share rising at the same time."
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: 95
resolution: Replaced the raw association ceiling with canonical semantic-share enforcement; retained diagnostics and documented truthful relationship kinds.
expected_result: Honest mixed graph growth passes; dilution below the floor fails across active and terminal items.
actual_result: Sandbox negative controls and live graph-composition gate pass; new Decision reference is structurally linked.
